# The answerer rule everywhere (#846 (finish shrinks a set), #1103
# (rework 2.1)): a handover proposes the matchmakers that answered its
# freeze, thinned to an odd count, also when the coordinator named the
# target set. The set in force then leaves its booked machines, and a set
# can shrink below the size the coordinator asked for. Rework 2.1 deletes
# the rule on finishes too; until then this mutant shows that the sets
# oracle and the heal predicate catch it where the caller named a target.
expect: caught
cause: sets: every tenant's set in force is its booked machines after chaos
cause: heal: a matchmaker set gets every member a live machine can take within the bound
file: crates/lib/paros-core/src/matchmaker/reconfigurer.rs
--- find
        let target = target
            .clone()
            .unwrap_or_else(|| odd_answerers(acks.keys().copied()));
--- replace
        let target = {
            let _ = target;
            odd_answerers(acks.keys().copied())
        };
--- end
